  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Kentwood is one of Raleigh's oldest and busiest courses — 18 short par 3s across 4,085 feet, with birdie opportunities on almost every hole. Since 1983 it's been the course where Raleigh players learn the game and where everyone goes for a quick, friendly round.",
    "Free to play with concrete tees and DISCatcher baskets, plus two extra practice baskets for putting warm-ups. It's a classic pitch-and-putt with real community character — expect a crowd and a welcoming one.",
    "Bring a putter and a midrange; that's the whole bag you need."
  ],

